<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:50:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Spain's parliament rejects housing bill as protests continue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13f5fcf8e99599c721f5e2c52c0f23df386136e59ee180a22d9d4e13b292438c</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:50:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-s-parliament-rejects-housing-bill-as-protests-continue/a-79522683--f3b2b2f36991.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-s-parliament-rejects-housing-bill-as-protests-continue/a-79522683?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's minority government suffered defeat in parliament as it tried to push through a pair of emergency measures aimed at making housing more affordable. A pensioner's eviction and protests led to the bid.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran accused of blocking SIM cards, digital access to silence dissent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a84c5958c6a5830ff1c8ae5504abd53e0a6f638fba1c12e0a4576bfbe061297</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:50:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-accused-of-blocking-sim-cards-digital-access-to-silence-dissent/a-79522440--050f09779478.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-accused-of-blocking-sim-cards-digital-access-to-silence-dissent/a-79522440?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has spoken with several Iranians who say their SIM cards, bank access and online accounts were blocked until they deleted critical content or pledged to stop activism.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Argentina launches cash-for-citizenship scheme</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccea6761bcf701b6d8d6d51c032984a647d636c0a54d3ca4f8f6e73f1c31cca5</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/argentina-launches-cash-for-citizenship-scheme/a-79520708--9871152522e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/argentina-launches-cash-for-citizenship-scheme/a-79520708?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investors seeking the fastest but most costly route to Argentine citizenship can choose between a non-refundable gift of $350,000, or buying a government bond for $800,000, if they think that will pay off in the end.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North and South Korea trade accusations over landmines that injured three soldiers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8aee5e704dc0ef46080e5e8d1d8a32e570c43da3b76428b60b9e77f9c0cb63ef</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-and-south-korea-trade-accusations-over-landmines-that-injured-three-soldiers/a-79503854--57b9ec347358.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-and-south-korea-trade-accusations-over-landmines-that-injured-three-soldiers/a-79503854?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A mine blast that injured three South Korean soldiers has renewed scrutiny of North Korea's actions along the border and raised questions about its strategic goals.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>This island in Kiribati could be the key to solve the Amelia Earhart mystery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:869b613d7f08cc4e27e271251174f5bcb24cb1457cd1b6fc713675a268e14e04</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-island-in-kiribati-could-be-the-key-to-solve-the-amelia-earhart-mystery/a-79517455--5be17a2d6029.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-island-in-kiribati-could-be-the-key-to-solve-the-amelia-earhart-mystery/a-79517455?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly 90 years after US aviator Amelia Earhart vanished over the Pacific, a new expedition to the remote island of Nikumaroro hopes a lagoon anomaly could finally reveal the fate of her missing aircraft.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Who could bring the warring sides to the negotiation table?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1643b4f18e171f8f5ae2152f5d23a1404612a176581fe421921de8f7eb1e9069</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-who-could-bring-the-warring-sides-to-the-negotiation-table/a-79475529--2936c02781db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-who-could-bring-the-warring-sides-to-the-negotiation-table/a-79475529?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia might be facing its most complex armed conflict in contemporary times. The fragile 2022 peace deal has collapsed. International mediators have failed. How will the country return to normal?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, South Korea clash over transfer of 2 North Korean prisoners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b2a9cdc54bdc2e4d2ad8cb83eb604d74c6f235aad33560568d40c6b7d850115</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T04:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-south-korea-clash-over-transfer-of-2-north-korean-prisoners/a-79508601--363762584d93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-south-korea-clash-over-transfer-of-2-north-korean-prisoners/a-79508601?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A diplomatic scandal has erupted over two North Korean prisoners of war, with South Korea demanding an apology from Ukraine. What's been the reaction in Kyiv?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Stock market scandal hits half a million investors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62cbbac3c34524f3199bbd86af8ac0ab9b1f6948c2698af63e4cd6d38b4ff361</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T04:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710--a0311f00dcbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Asset managers are alleged to have artificially inflated the value of their funds. Turkish authorities have made multiple arrests, and a leading AKP lawmakers has resigned.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU ministers mull new ways to curb irregular migration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cf7630770f4374456640a3ea7ecad6500cb5706884cae979952e40e8c30853b</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T00:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-ministers-mull-new-ways-to-curb-irregular-migration/a-79509375--720c002ac8dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-ministers-mull-new-ways-to-curb-irregular-migration/a-79509375?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The proposals include setting up so-called return hubs outside the EU and strengthening the border agency Frontex. Greece has even proposed temporarily suspending asylum applications in emergency situations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Latvians head to the polls with Russia on their minds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92d2a5fd0bf29894f53334b43d1bb8f72df7b3aa25af820745783bc6e69870d9</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T17:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/on-october-3-latvians-will-elect-a-new-parliament-_-with-russia-looming-large-over-the-campaign/a-79477614--649e559e634d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/latvians-head-to-the-polls-with-russia-on-their-minds/a-79477614?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On October 3, Latvians will elect a new parliament with Russia looming large over the campaign. Security fears dominate the agenda, but so does a debate over the economic cost of cutting ties with Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Renee Good's family sues Trump admin over fatal ICE shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:591978dbdbafe9a223b45519241e993cc78bbdd8fdafe49fd6b232f93481b530</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:49:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/renee-good-s-family-sues-trump-admin-over-fatal-ice-shooting/a-79504836--3b01ab91c959.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/renee-good-s-family-sues-trump-admin-over-fatal-ice-shooting/a-79504836?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The family of Renee Good, one of two US citizens fatally shot by federal immigration agents in Minneapolis in January, has sued President Donald Trump's administration alleging negligence and civil rights violations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
